<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Changnyeong County</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Changnyeong is a county in South Gyeongsang province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">South Korea</a>, on the east bank of the Nakdong river. It was the centre of Bihwa Gaya, one of the Gaya polities, before Silla absorbed it; a stele of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jinheung-of-silla">Jinheung of Silla</a> from 561 records his tour of the area. It also contains the Upo wetland and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gyo-dong-and-songhyeon-dong-tombs">Gyo-dong and Songhyeon-dong tombs</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/changnyeong-county.jpg" alt="Changnyeong County" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Taken by User:Visviva and released into the public domain. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Changnyeong_county_hall.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
